Open the ABOUT FIST sub-screen: drive a menu CLICK through activation -> screen-state machine -> the
modal dialog loop, faithfully reconstructing every base-loss / arg-drop on that path.  Clicking ABOUT
FIST now opens its dialog (panel + button row) crash-free and deterministically; the DOSBox reference is
ref/about_native320.png (tools/refcapture_click.sh).  The credit-TEXT elements are the remaining frontier
(the multi-element paint walk 1e88 + per-element paint-method arg threading -- see docs/stage1.md).

Sub-fixes (all asm-verified against re_out/fist_dat_image.bin):
- ea5a (activate method): param_2(elem)/param_3(base) are DGROUP near offsets, Ghidra deref'd them as
  host pointers -> SIGSEGV.  Reconstructed in the offset model; it writes DGROUP:0xf78e = the screen
  state (= [base+[elem+2]+1]); asm confirms aa4e returns the flags unchanged (push ax/pop ax around the
  c626 side-effect call) so (flags&4) gates activate-on-RELEASE.  Threaded the (flags,bb,base) args into
  the three [elem+0x4660] activate dispatches in the hit-test (the recurring indirect-vector arg-drop).
- 23bf: les di,ss:[0xea2c] far-ptr store composed (di|es<<16) as a flat host pointer -> base-loss.
- 92ea: element event method; di=[0x6d34] + its fields are DGROUP near offsets (host-ptr base-loss).
- e714 state jumptable: state 0xc -> 0xe969 = e39f(); 7088(4) (unrecovered fragment) -> reconstructed.
- 7088 (modal dialog loop): fixed the dialog-builder dispatch base-loss (word[DGROUP:(id-0x73ab)]), the
  Ghidra-mangled CF control flow, and added the cooperative INT-8 pump in the modal spin-wait; plus the
  id-indexed dispatch base-losses (71f8/7203/70fb: [id*2+const], [id-0x73a5]).
- 71de (dialog BG element method): threaded the [0x560] loader (idx 0x20 = FLDCOMP.MRL, the generic
  dialog panel) + [0x564] paint args -- same class as patch 110/094 (e3f8/e3bc menu bg).  Without it the
  loader built an empty name -> the panel resource never loaded -> RLE garbage.
  (The DOS 8.3 space-padded name "FLDCOMP .MRL" is canonicalized to "FLDCOMP.MRL" in the shim open_ci,
  re_out/fist_dos.c -- see that file; not part of this engine patch.)
